## 2. What I'd learn specifically in Wix Studio

I'd create a technical learning roadmap alongside the books.

| Skill | What I'd aim to master |
| --- | --- |
| Wix Studio | Layouts, sections, grids, stacks and breakpoints |
| Responsive design | Desktop, tablet and mobile optimization |
| CMS | Collections, dynamic pages, references and datasets |
| Velo | JavaScript, events and custom functionality |
| Wix SDK | Modern API integration and development |
| CSS | Custom styling, animations and advanced layouts |
| SEO | Metadata, redirects, structured data and indexing |
| Accessibility | Semantic structure, keyboard navigation and contrast |
| Performance | Image optimization, loading speed and Core Web Vitals |
| GitHub | Version control and managing code changes |

These aren't arbitrary skills. Wix's own professional developer and designer certification criteria emphasize responsive design, UX/UI, accessibility, SEO, performance, backend logic, API integrations and secure development.

