## 5. My final recommendation

If I were a junior Wix developer, this would be my priority:

| Priority | Area | Importance |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | UI/UX and visual design | Very high |
| 2 | Wix Studio mastery | Very high |
| 3 | HTML and CSS | Very high |
| 4 | JavaScript and Wix development | Very high |
| 5 | SEO and accessibility | High |
| 6 | CMS and dynamic websites | High |
| 7 | GitHub and software engineering | High |
| 8 | AI-assisted development | High |

One thing I'd avoid is becoming dependent on Wix's drag-and-drop tools or AI-generated code. Use them to work faster, but understand what you're building and how to troubleshoot it.

The real objective is to become a web developer who happens to specialize in Wix, rather than someone who only knows how to operate Wix.

That distinction will matter as your projects become more complex and you start working with bigger clients.

